This project addresses the critical challenge of detecting pneumonia from chest X-ray images using deep learning. The goal was to develop a reliable classification model by exploring and comparing different modern neural network architectures, handling class imbalance, and deploying the best-performing model as an interactive web application.

<br/>

Comparative Analysis & Solution

To find the most effective architecture, I trained and evaluated three different models: a baseline <b>ResNet-18</b>, a modern and efficient <b>EfficientNet-B0</b>, and a <b>Vision Transformer (ViT)</b>.

A key challenge was the significant class imbalance in the dataset, which initially caused a low recall for healthy patients. To solve this, I implemented a <b>Weighted Loss function</b> that successfully balanced the model's predictions and improved overall fairness and performance.

